{
  "id": "interface-echo",
  "title": "Every shipped interface family's generated echo reads its frame block and pass block back as the sentinels the host wrote",
  "binding": "Both legs boot an offscreen 256x256 world with seven pipeline rows, each running the generated echo pass of one shipped interface family's blocks: the ink simulation, visualize and finish passes (finish's block is also Moth's), the pipeline-package canary's tint, the film-grain shader set (whose block is also the post.sdf-film-grain package's), and the place and overlay engine packages. Each echo reads every member of its frame group block and its pass block through the declarations the engine generates for it, compares each word with the sentinel pipeline.sentinels makes the host write at that word's offset, and writes pixel i of a one-row image green when member i reads back exactly and red otherwise. The positive leg captures each row's one initialization frame after a reset with sentinels on, and every pixel of every row is green on both backends. The discriminating leg reloads every row onto its perturbed echo, the same echo over the generated declarations but with its last member's first word expecting the sentinel of the word after it, so each row's last pixel is red, the all-green observation turns red, and the members before it still read back. InterfaceEchoCanaryFixtureTests holds each echo's blocks to its targets' and each echo file to the generator.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": ["vulkan", "directx"],
  "requirements": ["gpu"],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
